  "notes": "Cross-dataset binary fault detection (healthy vs faulty). Transfer type: sim_to_real (source=DronePropA SIMULATED, target=TII REAL-PUBLIC). Level: time_broad_coral (feature_dim=54). Direction 1: DronePropA->TII (train=127: 40H/87F, test=99: 19H/80F). Direction 2: TII->DronePropA (train=99, test=127). DronePropA: F0=healthy, F1/F2/F3=faulty (127 flights, Simulink-generated). TII: class 0=healthy, class 1-4=faulty (99 missions, real experimental flights). Features: 6 channels (gyro xyz + accel xyz), sampling-rate invariant. No order-normalized (1P/2P) features: DronePropA 24.41 Hz peak is a control loop rate (1000/41 Hz), not propeller RPM (appears in motor_CMD and ESC telemetry, r=-0.753 vs throttle, pegged across all flights). TII ~40 Hz peak is real propeller RPM but varies 32-48 Hz. CORAL: linear Correlation Alignment (Sun & Saenko 2016). Scrutiny: permutation test (100 shuffles) on time_broad confirms 0.93 macro_F1 is real fault transfer (shuffled labels drop to 0.50, p<0.01), not domain leakage."
